# Files and folders NOT copied into the Docker image.
#
# When the image is built, the Astro Runtime base image runs `COPY . .`, which
# copies the whole project into /usr/local/airflow inside the image. Everything
# listed here is skipped, which:
#   - keeps secrets out of the image (.env is passed to the containers at
#     runtime by the Astro CLI instead)
#   - keeps the image small (no .venv, .git or caches)
#   - avoids needless rebuilds when only local files change (logs, editor settings)

astro
.git
.env
airflow_settings.yaml
logs/
.venv
airflow.db
airflow.cfg
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.vscode/
dashboard/
